// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/fpga/psp103_inv_ax7203.t27 -- the PSP103 CMOS inverter on the ALINX AX7203: 400 backward Euler steps, tt corner, tables in block RAM, one UART receipt line per step
; M3d of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #11208, success criterion SC-003). The inverter is the one of specs/analog/mos_psp103.t27 at 500 fF with
; dt = 100 ps (M3c, `q500_run`): the NMOS table and the PMOS table of sg13_lv_nmos / sg13_lv_pmos (PSP 103.6, 27 C, mos_tt) and the two drain-charge tables,
; read by the exact-integer bilinear reader of specs/analog/mos_table.t27 (`id_of`, `gds_cell`), solved at the output node by that file's backward Euler step
; (`board_step_q`: K_NEWTON = 3 Newton iterations, gate at Vdd before step 0, 0 V for steps 0 .. 199, Vdd for steps 200 .. 399, from the DC rest value of 3 units).
; This file is the board top of it. The four tables are NOT copied here: they come in by `use` from specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27 for the tests, and the board
; reads the same arrays from block RAM through that module's clocked port (see TABLES IN BLOCK RAM). What is written here is the machine, the receipt and the tests.
; Nothing of M3a/M3b/M3c, M0, M1b or the SAR top is edited; the pattern of specs/fpga/sar_adc_ax7203.t27 is followed: the restart request flags, the end of a line,
; the receipt as segments, the pins as attributes, the tests that run the machine beside the spec.
; -
; THE ARITHMETIC IS THE SPEC'S, ONE BIT A CLOCK. mos_table.t27 does a table read with 64-bit products (`blend`) and a Newton move with a 64-bit division
; (`newton_move`). The board has no DSP slice and no float, so the same integers are made in fabric by a shift-and-add multiplier and a restoring divider, a few
; hundred clocks a read, and tests compare every one with the spec's own function: the multiplier with `*`, the divider with `newton_move`, a whole read with
; `id_of` and `gds_cell` for all four tables, an iteration with `gq_pos`, `gq_neg` and `gq_deriv`, a step with `board_step_q`, the run with `run_fix_q`.
; A step is 14 table reads (2 for the previous step's charge, 3 x 4 for the iterations), each of which fetches the four nodes of its cell, then
;   lo = t00 (CELL - fx) + t10 fx    hi = t01 (CELL - fx) + t11 fx    id = (lo (CELL - fy) + hi fy + 2^39) >> 40            (six products)
;   gds = (dpos(t01, t00) (CELL - fx) + dpos(t11, t10) fx + 2^19) >> 20                                                  (two products)
; exactly as `blend` and `blend1` write them. Then p, n, d (gq_pos, gq_neg, gq_deriv), the quotient q = (|p - n| 2^20 + d / 2) / d by 47 restoring steps (the design
; bounds are g < 2^26 and d < 2^23; the run's largest are 1344396 and 1216890, a test measures both), and y moves down by q (p >= n) or up by q, clamped to 0 and Vdd.
; 1700 to 1960 clocks a step (about 19 us at 100 MHz); the line of the previous step takes 5.7 ms, so the machine is idle 99.7 % of the time and nothing is pipelined.
; -
; TABLES IN BLOCK RAM. `t27c gen-verilog` writes a const array of the module it compiles as a memory with its initial contents, and writes nothing for a name that
; came in by `use` (the reference is left undeclared, #8769 for functions; the same for arrays). So the memory lives where the arrays live: specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27
; has, next to TT_N, TT_P, TT_QD_N, TT_QD_P and the 400-word TT_RUN (the samples of the spec's own run), a clocked port `on_clock(addr, idx)` whose five outputs are
; registers: the word of each table at `addr` and the sample `idx`, as seen one clock earlier. This file's top instantiates that module (`AnalogMosPsp103Data`, an extern
; like the PLL) and the build reads both Verilog files. A read is therefore two clocks from the address register to the machine: the address is set, the RAM
; samples it, the machine takes the word. The machine runs the four nodes of a cell down that pipe one a clock. yosys maps a 625-word ROM to flip-flops and LUTs unless
; its memory carries `ram_style = "block"`, which `gen-verilog` does not write; the build script sets that attribute on the memories of the module (and says so in the table).
; -
; THE MACHINE, one phase a clock at 100 MHz (the PLL of M0 from the 200 MHz oscillator). A step:
;   P_STEP  y0 = y, the gate a of this step and a0 of the one before it, iteration 0
;   P_JOB   job jn picks the table (jt) and the point (jvg, jvd):  0 qp (Vdd - a0, Vdd - y0)   1 qn (a0, y0)   2 tn (a, y)   3 qn (a, y)   4 tp (Vdd - a, Vdd - y)   5 qp (Vdd - a, Vdd - y)
;   P_LIM P_CELL P_BASE   the point held to the table, its cell (cx, cy), the position in the cell (fx, fy), the address of node (cx, cy) = 25 cx + cy
;   P_RD1 .. P_RD5        the four nodes, t00 t10 t01 t11, down the two-clock pipe of the RAM
;   P_LO1 .. P_G3         the eight products by P_MUL (the multiplier: add x when the weight's low bit is set, shift, until the weight is 0)
;   P_ACC   job 0 and 1 keep their id (c1, c2); jobs 2 .. 5 add id and gds to p = y + c1 + .., n = y0 + c2 + .. and d = CELL + ..  (P_IT starts an iteration)
;   P_PN P_DIV P_UPD      q, then y; the third iteration ends the step
; then the verdict (y against the spec's sample), the order-sensitive fold of the samples, and the line. No clock chains more than one add, one compare or one table mux.
; -
; THE RESTART. As the SAR top: the button and LOCKED pass two registers; while they say no the request flags `fin` and `hard` are set every clock and the next clock
; puts the machine at step 0, line 0, y at the rest value. A finished line sets `fin` alone and the next clock starts the next step. After step 399 the board goes back to
; step 0 (y at the rest value, the fold cleared), so the 400 lines repeat for as long as the capture runs (L counts on). THE END OF A LINE is the SAR top's: `fin` is set
; GAP_BITS bit times after the LF's stop bit has ended.
; -
; THE RECEIPT. 115200 baud on N15 (divider 868 from 100 MHz), one line per step, M0's grammar:
;   T27 PSP N=<3 hex> Y=<7 hex> E=<7 hex> S=<16 hex> L=<4 hex> PASS
; N the step (0 .. 18F), Y the output the board computed after it (units of 2^-24 V, 59.6 nV), E the spec's sample for it (TT_RUN, from the RAM), S the order-sensitive
; fold of the board's samples of this round (N = 0 .. this one; at N = 18F it is EXP_S_TT_Q, 0x215DC5EAC4C48576), L the lines since the button. PASS when Y equals E, else
; FAIL. LEDs (active low) as M0: B13 the line is being sent, C13 FAIL, D14 PASS, D15 a heartbeat. The button T6 resets.
; -
; THE NEGATIVE CONTROL. The same top with the ss tables in the tt top: TT_N, TT_P, TT_QD_N, TT_QD_P read as SS_N, SS_P, SS_QD_N, SS_QD_P, the rest value and the
; samples E unchanged. The spec's own run on those tables (`run_fix_q`, a test) differs from the tt run at 323 of the 400 steps, every step but 145 and 324 .. 399 (the
; ss output crosses the tt one once, and both are back at the rest value of 3 units from step 324), so a build with the ss tables prints FAIL on those 323 lines and PASS on
; the other 77; its fold at N = 18F is the ss run's, EXP_S_SS_Q = 0x987F22AC4132345B, and its Y on every line is the ss run's sample.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. This board, running RTL generated from this file and from the data module, solved the backward Euler step of the 500 fF PSP103 inverter at the
; tt corner from the foundry-model tables 400 times and produced, at every step, the sample the spec's fixed-point run produces (the tests compare the machine with
; the spec's functions at every level above, and the whole run word for word, including the clocks of the line at the real baud divider). By mos_psp103.t27 that run
; is within 0.020 % and 0.0041 % of ngspice's two 50 % delays at tt.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about the circuit beyond that spec: a table model of PSP103, tt only here (the other four corners are other tables, not built), 27 C, one
; gate waveform (two levels, an ideal step), one load. The machine reads any gate voltage inside 0 .. Vdd but the run only ever uses the two rails. Nothing about speed
; (19 us a step is not a comparison with ngspice: ngspice's wall time is mostly its start-up and this board's is mostly the UART), power, noise or another node count.
; The expected samples are the spec's own output stored in the RAM: a PASS says the board agrees with the spec, not with ngspice. ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module FpgaPsp103Inv;

use analog::linear;
use analog::mos_table::{VDD, CELL, CELL_BITS, HALF_Q, NODES, K_NEWTON, RUN_STEPS, gate_at, lim, cell_of, frac_of, dpos, mag_diff, id_of, gds_cell, blend, blend1, newton_move, gq_pos, gq_neg, gq_deriv, board_step_q, run_fix_q};
use analog::mos_psp103::{dc_out, EXP_S_TT_Q, EXP_S_SS_Q};
use analog::mos_psp103_data::{TT_N, TT_P, TT_QD_N, TT_QD_P, TT_RUN, SS_N, SS_P, SS_QD_N, SS_QD_P};
use fpga::rc_filter_ax7203;

pub const KIND : str = "board-cell";
pub const ID : str = "fpga/psp103_inv_ax7203";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "specs/analog/mos_psp103.t27 (M3c q500_run), specs/analog/mos_table.t27 (run_fix_q), specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27 (tt tables, TT_RUN)";
pub const BOARD : str = "ALINX AX7203";
pub const PART : str = "xc7a200tfbg484-2";

; --- the run, as the board holds it ----------------------------------------------------------------
/// The steps of a round (mos_table's RUN_STEPS, as a u16), and the index of the last.
pub const STEPS_N : u16 = 400;
pub const STEP_LAST : u16 = 399;
/// The Newton iterations of a step (mos_table's K_NEWTON, as a u8) and the table reads of an iteration (jobs 2 .. 5).
pub const ITERS : u8 = 3;
pub const JOB_LAST : u8 = 5;
/// The DC rest value of the tt tables (dc_out(TT_N, TT_P, Vdd)): the output before step 0, 3 units.
pub const REST_TT : u32 = 3;
/// The idle bit times after the last stop bit of a line, before the next step starts.
pub const GAP_BITS : u8 = 2;
/// The characters of a line, and its segments.
pub const LINE_LEN : usize = 66;
pub const PSP_SEGS : u8 = 7;
/// The restoring divider: bits of the dividend (g 2^20 + d / 2 is under 2^47), and the bounds the run keeps g and d under.
pub const DIV_BITS : u8 = 47;
pub const G_BOUND : u32 = 67108864;
pub const D_BOUND : u32 = 8388608;
/// 2^19: the rounding of a gds read.
pub const HALF_G : u64 = 524288;
/// The negative control: the steps at which the ss tables give the tt sample (145, and 324 .. 399), so 323 FAIL lines.
pub const CTRL_FAILS : u32 = 323;
pub const CTRL_PASS_AT : u16 = 145;
pub const CTRL_SETTLED_FROM : u16 = 324;

; --- the machine --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const P_STEP : u8 = 0;
pub const P_JOB : u8 = 1;
pub const P_LIM : u8 = 2;
pub const P_CELL : u8 = 3;
pub const P_BASE : u8 = 4;
pub const P_RD1 : u8 = 5;
pub const P_RD2 : u8 = 6;
pub const P_RD3 : u8 = 7;
pub const P_RD4 : u8 = 8;
pub const P_RD5 : u8 = 9;
pub const P_LO1 : u8 = 10;
pub const P_MUL : u8 = 11;
pub const P_LO2 : u8 = 12;
pub const P_LO3 : u8 = 13;
pub const P_HI2 : u8 = 14;
pub const P_HI3 : u8 = 15;
pub const P_W2 : u8 = 16;
pub const P_W3 : u8 = 17;
pub const P_G2 : u8 = 18;
pub const P_G3 : u8 = 19;
pub const P_ACC : u8 = 20;
pub const P_IT : u8 = 21;
pub const P_PN : u8 = 22;
pub const P_DIV : u8 = 23;
pub const P_UPD : u8 = 24;

; --- facts --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The gate of the step before step n: Vdd before step 0 (the circuit rests with its gate high), else the gate of step n - 1.
pub fn prev_gate(n: u16) -> u32 {
    if (n == 0) { return VDD; }
    return gate_at(((n - 1) as u32));
}

/// The table job jn reads: 0 tn, 1 tp, 2 qn, 3 qp (the order of the RAM's outputs).
pub fn job_table(jn: u8) -> u8 {
    if (jn == 0) { return 3; }
    if (jn == 1) { return 2; }
    if (jn == 2) { return 0; }
    if (jn == 3) { return 2; }
    if (jn == 4) { return 1; }
    return 3;
}

/// The gate coordinate of job jn: the previous gate for the two charge terms of the previous point, this gate for the NMOS side, its mirror for the PMOS side.
pub fn job_vg(jn: u8, ga: u32, ga0: u32) -> u32 {
    if (jn == 0) { return VDD - ga0; }
    if (jn == 1) { return ga0; }
    if (jn == 2 or jn == 3) { return ga; }
    return VDD - ga;
}

/// The drain coordinate of job jn: the previous output y0 for jobs 0 and 1, the iterate y for the others, mirrored for the PMOS side.
pub fn job_vd(jn: u8, y: u32, y0: u32) -> u32 {
    if (jn == 0) { return VDD - y0; }
    if (jn == 1) { return y0; }
    if (jn == 2 or jn == 3) { return y; }
    return VDD - y;
}

/// The word of the table jt among the four the RAM answers with.
pub fn pick_word(jt: u8, tn: u32, tp: u32, qn: u32, qp: u32) -> u32 {
    if (jt == 0) { return tn; }
    if (jt == 1) { return tp; }
    if (jt == 2) { return qn; }
    return qp;
}

/// The address of node (cx, cy): 25 cx + cy, as shifts and adds (25 = 16 + 8 + 1).
pub fn node_base(cx: u32, cy: u32) -> u16 {
    return ((cx << 4) + (cx << 3) + cx + cy) as u16;
}

/// The remainder register of the divider after it takes the next bit of the dividend (bit 46 of dq).
pub fn div_r2(rem: u32, dq: u64) -> u32 {
    return (rem << 1) | (((dq >> 46) & 1) as u32);
}

/// PASS when the board's sample equals the spec's.
pub fn psp_verdict(y: u32, e: u32) -> u8 {
    if (y == e) { return V_PASS; }
    return V_FAIL;
}

; --- the receipt: M0's line, with the fields of a step ----------------------------------------------------
; hex_digit and pass_fail_char (board_receipt), frame, prefix_char (M0) are shared; the segments are these:
;   0 "T27 PSP"   1 " N=" + 3 hex   2 " Y=" + 7 hex   3 " E=" + 7 hex   4 " S=" + 16 hex   5 " L=" + 4 hex   6 " PASS\r\n"

/// The key letter of field s (1..5): N Y E S L.
pub fn psp_key(s: u8) -> u8 {
    if (s == 1) { return 78; }
    if (s == 2) { return 89; }
    if (s == 3) { return 69; }
    if (s == 4) { return 83; }
    return 76;
}

/// The hex digits of field s (1..5).
pub fn psp_width(s: u8) -> u8 {
    if (s == 1) { return 3; }
    if (s == 2 or s == 3) { return 7; }
    if (s == 4) { return 16; }
    return 4;
}

/// The last position of segment s: the prefix and the verdict have 7 characters, a field has " X=" and its digits.
pub fn psp_seg_last(s: u8) -> u8 {
    if (s == 0) { return 6; }
    if (s == PSP_SEGS - 1) { return 6; }
    return 2 + psp_width(s);
}

/// Character p of "T27 PSP": M0's "T27 " and the name.
pub fn psp_prefix(p: u8) -> u8 {
    if (p < 4) { return prefix_char(p); }
    if (p == 4) { return 80; }
    if (p == 5) { return 83; }
    return 80;
}

/// The character at segment s, position p; `fsr` holds the field being written, its next nibble on top.
pub fn psp_char(s: u8, p: u8, fsr: u64, v: u8) -> u8 {
    if (s == 0) { return psp_prefix(p); }
    if (s == PSP_SEGS - 1) { return pass_fail_char(v, p); }
    if (p == 0) { return 32; }
    if (p == 1) { return psp_key(s); }
    if (p == 2) { return 61; }
    return hex_digit((fsr >> 60) as u8);
}

/// Field s (1..5) placed at the top of the 64-bit register, so that its first digit is nibble 15: 4 * (16 - width) bits up.
pub fn psp_top(s: u8, n: u16, y: u32, e: u32, sum: u64, l: u32) -> u64 {
    if (s == 1) { return (n as u64) << 52; }
    if (s == 2) { return (y as u64) << 36; }
    if (s == 3) { return (e as u64) << 36; }
    if (s == 4) { return sum; }
    return (l as u64) << 48;
}

; --- the board ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// A differential input buffer (the 200 MHz oscillator on R4/T4).
pub struct IbufdsOut { O: bool }
pub fn IBUFDS(I: bool, IB: bool) -> IbufdsOut {}

/// The tables' RAM: the clocked port of specs/analog/mos_psp103_data.t27, generated by `t27c gen-verilog`. Its outputs are the word of TT_N, TT_P, TT_QD_N, TT_QD_P at
/// `addr` and the sample TT_RUN[idx], each a register. rst_n and en are the module's own inputs, tied high here.
pub struct RomOut { tn: u32, tp: u32, qn: u32, qp: u32, ex: u32 }
pub fn AnalogMosPsp103Data(clk_: bool, rst_n_: bool, en_: bool, addr: u16, idx: u16) -> RomOut {}

; --- the pins in --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
const clk200_p : bool = undefined;
const clk200_p_LOC : str = "R4";
const clk200_p_IOSTANDARD : str = "DIFF_SSTL15";
const clk200_n : bool = undefined;
const clk200_n_LOC : str = "T4";
const clk200_n_IOSTANDARD : str = "DIFF_SSTL15";
const cpu_reset_n : bool = undefined;
const cpu_reset_n_LOC : str = "T6";
const cpu_reset_n_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS15";

; --- the clock and the reset: M0's, unchanged ---------------------------------------------------
const clkbuf : IbufdsOut = IBUFDS(clk200_p, clk200_n);
const clkbuf_O_PERIOD_PS : u32 = 5000;
const pll : PllOut = PLLE2_ADV(clkbuf.O, pll.CLKFBOUT, false, false, 5.0, 0.01, 8, 1, 16, 0, "FALSE");
const gclk : BufgOut = BUFG(pll.CLKOUT0);
const gclk_O_PERIOD_PS : u32 = 10000;

const btn : IbufOut = IBUF(cpu_reset_n);

// No asynchronous reset (M0, M1b, the SAR top): the button and LOCKED pass two registers, they set the restart request, and on the next
// edge on_clock puts the machine back at its start.
const clk : bool = gclk.O;
const rst_n : bool = true;
const en : bool = true;

; --- the registers ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
var st : u8 = 0;
var ph : u8 = 0;
var stp : u16 = 0;
var r_y : u32 = 3;
var r_y0 : u32 = 3;
var r_ga : u32 = 0;
var r_ga0 : u32 = 0;
var r_it : u8 = 0;
var r_jn : u8 = 0;
var r_jt : u8 = 0;
var r_vg : u32 = 0;
var r_vd : u32 = 0;
var r_gv : u32 = 0;
var r_dv : u32 = 0;
var r_cx : u32 = 0;
var r_cy : u32 = 0;
var r_fx : u32 = 0;
var r_fy : u32 = 0;
var r_ad : u16 = 0;
var r_t0 : u32 = 0;
var r_t1 : u32 = 0;
var r_t2 : u32 = 0;
var r_t3 : u32 = 0;
var r_mx : u64 = 0;
var r_mw : u32 = 0;
var r_mret : u8 = 0;
var r_acc : u64 = 0;
var r_lo : u64 = 0;
var r_hi : u64 = 0;
var r_id : u32 = 0;
var r_gd : u32 = 0;
var r_c1 : u32 = 0;
var r_c2 : u32 = 0;
var r_sp : u32 = 0;
var r_sn : u32 = 0;
var r_sd : u32 = 0;
var r_up : bool = false;
var r_dq : u64 = 0;
var r_dvs : u32 = 0;
var r_rem : u32 = 0;
var r_qt : u32 = 0;
var r_dc : u8 = 0;
var cs : u64 = 0;
var verdict : u8 = 1;
var baud_div : u16 = 868;
var tx_cnt : u16 = 0;
var tx_sh : u16 = 1023;
var tx_left : u8 = 0;
var seg : u8 = 0;
var upos : u8 = 0;
var fsr : u64 = 0;
var lines : u32 = 0;
var last : bool = false;
var gap : u8 = 0;
var hard : bool = false;
var fin : bool = false;
var hb : u32 = 0;
var go0 : bool = false;
var go1 : bool = false;

; --- the tables' RAM: an instance of the data module, the address and the sample index are registers --------
const rom : RomOut = AnalogMosPsp103Data(clk, true, true, r_ad, stp);

; --- the pins out: registers, set from the state one clock later (a pub var is an output reg) ----
pub var uart_tx : bool = true;
const uart_tx_LOC : str = "N15";
const uart_tx_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS33";
pub var led_0 : bool = true;
const led_0_LOC : str = "B13";
const led_0_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS33";
pub var led_1 : bool = true;
const led_1_LOC : str = "C13";
const led_1_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS33";
pub var led_2 : bool = true;
const led_2_LOC : str = "D14";
const led_2_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS33";
pub var led_3 : bool = false;
const led_3_LOC : str = "D15";
const led_3_IOSTANDARD : str = "LVCMOS33";

// Every var is read before it is written, so the test's order and the clock edge agree.
fn on_clock(pll_LOCKED: bool, btn_O: bool, rom_tn: u32, rom_tp: u32, rom_qn: u32, rom_qp: u32, rom_ex: u32) {
    uart_tx = st != ST_REPORT or (tx_sh & 1) == 1;
    led_0 = st != ST_REPORT;
    led_1 = !(st == ST_REPORT and verdict == V_FAIL);
    led_2 = !(st == ST_REPORT and verdict == V_PASS);
    led_3 = ((hb >> 27) & 1) == 1;
    hb = hb + 1;
    if (fin) {
        if (hard) {
            stp = 0;
            r_y = REST_TT;
            lines = 0;
            cs = 0;
            hard = false;
        } else {
            if (stp == STEP_LAST) {
                stp = 0;
                r_y = REST_TT;
                cs = 0;
            } else {
                stp = stp + 1;
            }
        }
        st = ST_RUN;
        ph = P_STEP;
        verdict = V_FAIL;
        tx_cnt = 0;
        tx_sh = 1023;
        tx_left = 0;
        seg = 0;
        upos = 0;
        fsr = 0;
        last = false;
        gap = 0;
        fin = false;
    } else if (st == ST_RUN) {
        if (ph == P_STEP) {
            r_y0 = r_y;
            r_ga = gate_at((stp as u32));
            r_ga0 = prev_gate(stp);
            r_it = 0;
            r_jn = 0;
            ph = P_JOB;
        } else if (ph == P_JOB) {
            r_vg = job_vg(r_jn, r_ga, r_ga0);
            r_vd = job_vd(r_jn, r_y, r_y0);
            r_jt = job_table(r_jn);
            ph = P_LIM;
        } else if (ph == P_LIM) {
            r_gv = lim(r_vg);
            r_dv = lim(r_vd);
            ph = P_CELL;
        } else if (ph == P_CELL) {
            r_cx = cell_of(r_gv);
            r_cy = cell_of(r_dv);
            r_fx = frac_of(r_gv);
            r_fy = frac_of(r_dv);
            ph = P_BASE;
        } else if (ph == P_BASE) {
            r_ad = node_base(r_cx, r_cy);
            ph = P_RD1;
        } else if (ph == P_RD1) {
            r_ad = r_ad + 25;
            ph = P_RD2;
        } else if (ph == P_RD2) {
            r_t0 = pick_word(r_jt, rom_tn, rom_tp, rom_qn, rom_qp);
            r_ad = r_ad - 24;
            ph = P_RD3;
        } else if (ph == P_RD3) {
            r_t1 = pick_word(r_jt, rom_tn, rom_tp, rom_qn, rom_qp);
            r_ad = r_ad + 25;
            ph = P_RD4;
        } else if (ph == P_RD4) {
            r_t2 = pick_word(r_jt, rom_tn, rom_tp, rom_qn, rom_qp);
            ph = P_RD5;
        } else if (ph == P_RD5) {
            r_t3 = pick_word(r_jt, rom_tn, rom_tp, rom_qn, rom_qp);
            ph = P_LO1;
        } else if (ph == P_LO1) {
            r_acc = 0;
            r_mx = r_t0 as u64;
            r_mw = CELL - r_fx;
            r_mret = P_LO2;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_MUL) {
            if (r_mw == 0) {
                ph = r_mret;
            } else {
                if ((r_mw & 1) == 1) { r_acc = r_acc + r_mx; }
                r_mx = r_mx << 1;
                r_mw = r_mw >> 1;
            }
        } else if (ph == P_LO2) {
            r_mx = r_t1 as u64;
            r_mw = r_fx;
            r_mret = P_LO3;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_LO3) {
            r_lo = r_acc;
            r_acc = 0;
            r_mx = r_t2 as u64;
            r_mw = CELL - r_fx;
            r_mret = P_HI2;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_HI2) {
            r_mx = r_t3 as u64;
            r_mw = r_fx;
            r_mret = P_HI3;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_HI3) {
            r_hi = r_acc;
            r_acc = HALF_Q;
            r_mx = r_lo;
            r_mw = CELL - r_fy;
            r_mret = P_W2;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_W2) {
            r_mx = r_hi;
            r_mw = r_fy;
            r_mret = P_W3;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_W3) {
            r_id = (r_acc >> 40) as u32;
            r_acc = HALF_G;
            r_mx = dpos((r_t2 as u64), (r_t0 as u64));
            r_mw = CELL - r_fx;
            r_mret = P_G2;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_G2) {
            r_mx = dpos((r_t3 as u64), (r_t1 as u64));
            r_mw = r_fx;
            r_mret = P_G3;
            ph = P_MUL;
        } else if (ph == P_G3) {
            r_gd = (r_acc >> 20) as u32;
            ph = P_ACC;
        } else if (ph == P_ACC) {
            if (r_jn == 0) {
                r_c1 = r_id;
                r_jn = 1;
                ph = P_JOB;
            } else if (r_jn == 1) {
                r_c2 = r_id;
                r_jn = 2;
                ph = P_IT;
            } else if (r_jn == 2 or r_jn == 3) {
                r_sp = r_sp + r_id;
                r_sd = r_sd + r_gd;
                r_jn = r_jn + 1;
                ph = P_JOB;
            } else if (r_jn == 4) {
                r_sn = r_sn + r_id;
                r_sd = r_sd + r_gd;
                r_jn = 5;
                ph = P_JOB;
            } else {
                r_sn = r_sn + r_id;
                r_sd = r_sd + r_gd;
                ph = P_PN;
            }
        } else if (ph == P_IT) {
            r_sp = r_y + r_c1;
            r_sn = r_y0 + r_c2;
            r_sd = CELL;
            ph = P_JOB;
        } else if (ph == P_PN) {
            r_up = r_sp >= r_sn;
            r_dq = (((mag_diff(r_sp, r_sn)) as u64) << 20) + ((r_sd as u64) >> 1);
            r_dvs = r_sd;
            r_rem = 0;
            r_qt = 0;
            r_dc = 0;
            ph = P_DIV;
        } else if (ph == P_DIV) {
            if (div_r2(r_rem, r_dq) >= r_dvs) {
                r_rem = div_r2(r_rem, r_dq) - r_dvs;
                r_qt = (r_qt << 1) | 1;
            } else {
                r_rem = div_r2(r_rem, r_dq);
                r_qt = r_qt << 1;
            }
            r_dq = r_dq << 1;
            if (r_dc == DIV_BITS - 1) { ph = P_UPD; }
            r_dc = r_dc + 1;
        } else {
            if (r_up) {
                if (r_qt >= r_y) { r_y = 0; } else { r_y = r_y - r_qt; }
            } else {
                if (r_qt >= VDD - r_y) { r_y = VDD; } else { r_y = r_y + r_qt; }
            }
            if (r_it == ITERS - 1) {
                st = ST_JUDGE;
            } else {
                r_jn = 2;
                ph = P_IT;
            }
            r_it = r_it + 1;
        }
    } else if (st == ST_JUDGE) {
        verdict = psp_verdict(r_y, rom_ex);
        cs = fold(cs, r_y);
        st = ST_REPORT;
    } else {
        if (tx_cnt != 0) {
            tx_cnt = tx_cnt - 1;
        } else {
            tx_cnt = baud_div - 1;
            if (tx_left != 0) {
                tx_sh = (tx_sh >> 1) | 512;
                tx_left = tx_left - 1;
            } else if (last) {
                if (gap == GAP_BITS) {
                    fin = true;
                } else {
                    gap = gap + 1;
                }
            } else {
                tx_sh = frame(psp_char(seg, upos, fsr, verdict));
                tx_left = 9;
                if (upos == psp_seg_last(seg)) {
                    fsr = psp_top(seg + 1, stp, r_y, rom_ex, cs, lines);
                    upos = 0;
                    if (seg == PSP_SEGS - 1) {
                        seg = 0;
                        lines = lines + 1;
                        last = true;
                    } else {
                        seg = seg + 1;
                    }
                } else {
                    if (seg != 0 and seg != PSP_SEGS - 1 and upos >= 3) { fsr = fsr << 4; }
                    upos = upos + 1;
                }
            }
        }
    }
    if (!go1) {
        fin = true;
        hard = true;
    }
    go1 = go0;
    go0 = pll_LOCKED and btn_O;
}

; --- test-only helpers (the hardware does not reach them) ----------------------------------------------

/// The RAM as the tests model it: its five output registers, and which corner's tables it holds (false: tt, true: ss, the control).
var m_tn : u32 = 0;
var m_tp : u32 = 0;
var m_qn : u32 = 0;
var m_qp : u32 = 0;
var m_ex : u32 = 0;
var m_ss : bool = false;

fn rom_n(a: u16) -> u32 {
    if (m_ss) { return SS_N[a as usize]; }
    return TT_N[a as usize];
}

fn rom_p(a: u16) -> u32 {
    if (m_ss) { return SS_P[a as usize]; }
    return TT_P[a as usize];
}

fn rom_qn(a: u16) -> u32 {
    if (m_ss) { return SS_QD_N[a as usize]; }
    return TT_QD_N[a as usize];
}

fn rom_qp(a: u16) -> u32 {
    if (m_ss) { return SS_QD_P[a as usize]; }
    return TT_QD_P[a as usize];
}

/// The table jt of the tt corner as a slice, for the spec's own reader.
fn tab_of(t: u8) -> []const u32 {
    if (t == 0) { return &TT_N; }
    if (t == 1) { return &TT_P; }
    if (t == 2) { return &TT_QD_N; }
    return &TT_QD_P;
}

/// One clock of the board with the RAM beside it: the machine sees the words the RAM registered at the last edge, and the RAM registers the words of the
/// address and the sample index the machine held before this edge (a synchronous read).
fn tick() {
    const a : u16 = r_ad;
    const s : u16 = stp;
    on_clock(true, true, m_tn, m_tp, m_qn, m_qp, m_ex);
    m_tn = rom_n(a);
    m_tp = rom_p(a);
    m_qn = rom_qn(a);
    m_qp = rom_qp(a);
    m_ex = TT_RUN[s as usize];
}

/// The machine as the button leaves it, then step k selected with the output of the step before it (the start of step k).
fn boot_at(k: u16) {
    go0 = true;
    go1 = false;
    m_tn = 0;
    m_tp = 0;
    m_qn = 0;
    m_qp = 0;
    m_ex = 0;
    tick();
    tick();
    stp = k;
    if (k == 0) {
        r_y = REST_TT;
    } else {
        r_y = TT_RUN[(k - 1) as usize];
    }
}

/// Runs the machine from where it stands to the end of the step (ST_JUDGE); the clocks it took.
fn run_to_judge() -> u32 {
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (st == ST_RUN and n < 100000) {
        tick();
        n = n + 1;
    }
    return n;
}

/// Runs until the machine is at phase p, or n clocks have passed; the clocks it took.
fn run_to_phase(p: u8, limit: u32) -> u32 {
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (ph != p and n < limit) {
        tick();
        n = n + 1;
    }
    return n;
}

/// The value of the n hex digits of buf from position at.
fn hex_at(buf: []const u8, at: usize, n: usize) -> u64 {
    var v : u64 = 0;
    var k : usize = 0;
    while (k < n) {
        const c : u8 = buf[at + k];
        if (c >= 65) {
            v = (v << 4) | ((c - 55) as u64);
        } else {
            v = (v << 4) | ((c - 48) as u64);
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    return v;
}

/// The next word of a linear congruential sequence (the tests' own pseudo-random points).
fn lcg(x: u32) -> u32 {
    return x *% 1664525 +% 1013904223;
}

; --- the tests ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

test the_constants_are_the_specs {
    assert_eq(STEPS_N as u32, RUN_STEPS);
    assert_eq((STEP_LAST as u32) + 1, RUN_STEPS);
    assert_eq(ITERS as u32, K_NEWTON);
    assert_eq(dc_out(&TT_N, &TT_P, VDD), REST_TT);
    assert_eq(HALF_G, (CELL >> 1) as u64);
    assert_eq(HALF_Q, 549755813888);
    assert_eq(CELL, 1 << 20);
    assert_eq(NODES, 25);
    assert_eq((DIV_BITS as u32), 47);
    assert_eq(CTRL_FAILS + 77, RUN_STEPS);
    // the run the RAM holds is the spec's run, word for word
    var out : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    var res : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    const s : u64 = run_fix_q(&TT_N, &TT_P, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, K_NEWTON, REST_TT, VDD, false, &out, &res);
    assert_eq(s, EXP_S_TT_Q);
    var i : usize = 0;
    var f : u64 = 0;
    var worst : u32 = 0;
    while (i < 400) {
        assert_eq(TT_RUN[i], out[i]);
        f = fold(f, TT_RUN[i]);
        if (res[i] > worst) { worst = res[i]; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(f, EXP_S_TT_Q);
    // the last Newton residual is at most 2 units at every step (mos_psp103.t27): the board's three iterations are enough
    assert(worst <= 2);
    assert(worst >= 1);
    // a changed sample is seen
    assert(TT_RUN[100] + 1 != out[100]);
}

test the_gate_the_jobs_and_the_addresses_are_the_specs {
    assert_eq(prev_gate(0), VDD);
    assert_eq(prev_gate(1), 0);
    assert_eq(prev_gate(200), 0);
    assert_eq(prev_gate(201), VDD);
    assert_eq(prev_gate(399), VDD);
    var n : u16 = 0;
    while (n < STEPS_N) {
        if (n > 0) { assert_eq(prev_gate(n), gate_at(((n - 1) as u32))); }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    // the six jobs: which table, at which point
    assert_eq(job_table(0), 3);
    assert_eq(job_table(1), 2);
    assert_eq(job_table(2), 0);
    assert_eq(job_table(3), 2);
    assert_eq(job_table(4), 1);
    assert_eq(job_table(5), 3);
    assert_eq(job_vg(0, 100, 7), VDD - 7);
    assert_eq(job_vd(0, 100, 7), VDD - 7);
    assert_eq(job_vg(1, 100, 7), 7);
    assert_eq(job_vd(1, 100, 7), 7);
    assert_eq(job_vg(2, 100, 7), 100);
    assert_eq(job_vd(2, 100, 7), 100);
    assert_eq(job_vg(3, 100, 7), 100);
    assert_eq(job_vd(3, 100, 7), 100);
    assert_eq(job_vg(4, 100, 7), VDD - 100);
    assert_eq(job_vd(4, 100, 7), VDD - 100);
    assert_eq(job_vg(5, 100, 7), VDD - 100);
    assert_eq(job_vd(5, 100, 7), VDD - 100);
    assert_eq(JOB_LAST, 5);
    assert_eq(pick_word(0, 10, 20, 30, 40), 10);
    assert_eq(pick_word(1, 10, 20, 30, 40), 20);
    assert_eq(pick_word(2, 10, 20, 30, 40), 30);
    assert_eq(pick_word(3, 10, 20, 30, 40), 40);
    // 25 cx + cy by shifts, for every cell of the grid and the node one past it
    var cxx : u32 = 0;
    var cyy : u32 = 0;
    while (cxx < 24) {
        cyy = 0;
        while (cyy < 24) {
            assert_eq(node_base(cxx, cyy) as u32, cxx * NODES + cyy);
            assert(((node_base(cxx, cyy) as u32) + NODES + 1) < 625);
            cyy = cyy + 1;
        }
        cxx = cxx + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(psp_verdict(5, 5), V_PASS);
    assert_eq(psp_verdict(5, 6), V_FAIL);
}

test the_shift_and_add_multiplier_is_the_product {
    var xs : [9]u64 = [0, 1, 3, 4095, 1048575, 1048576, 2097151, 8388607, 8796093022207];
    var ws : [9]u32 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 12345, 524287, 1048575, 1048576, 1000003];
    var i : usize = 0;
    var j : usize = 0;
    var n : u32 = 0;
    var longest : u32 = 0;
    while (i < 9) {
        j = 0;
        while (j < 9) {
            boot_at(0);
            r_acc = 77;
            r_mx = xs[i];
            r_mw = ws[j];
            r_mret = P_LO3;
            ph = P_MUL;
            n = run_to_phase(P_LO3, 100);
            assert_eq(r_acc, 77 + xs[i] * (ws[j] as u64));
            if (n > longest) { longest = n; }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    // a product of a weight under 2^21 takes at most 22 clocks, so a read stays a few hundred
    assert_eq(longest, 22);
}

test the_restoring_divider_is_the_specs_newton_move {
    var gs : [10]u32 = [0, 1, 2, 12345, 1048576, 33554432, 25165823, 67108863, 500000, 3];
    var ds : [8]u32 = [1048576, 1048577, 1500000, 2097159, 4194304, 8388607, 1310720, 3000001];
    var i : usize = 0;
    var j : usize = 0;
    var longest : u32 = 0;
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (i < 10) {
        j = 0;
        while (j < 8) {
            boot_at(0);
            r_sp = gs[i] + 1000;
            r_sn = 1000;
            r_sd = ds[j];
            ph = P_PN;
            n = run_to_phase(P_UPD, 100);
            assert_eq(r_qt, newton_move(gs[i], ds[j] as u64));
            assert(r_up);
            // and the other direction
            r_sp = 1000;
            r_sn = gs[i] + 1000;
            ph = P_PN;
            n = n + run_to_phase(P_UPD, 100);
            assert_eq(r_qt, newton_move(gs[i], ds[j] as u64));
            if (gs[i] > 0) { assert(!r_up); }
            if (n > longest) { longest = n; }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    // P_PN and 47 clocks of P_DIV, twice here (once a direction); the dividend fits 47 bits
    assert_eq(longest, 2 * (1 + (DIV_BITS as u32)));
    assert(((67108863 as u64) << 20) + 4194303 < (1 << 47));
}

test a_table_read_is_the_specs_id_and_gds_for_all_four_tables {
    var vgs : [12]u32 = [0, 1, 524288, 1048575, 1048576, 1048577, 5255225, 14631487, 24117248, 25165823, 25165824, 25200000];
    var vds : [14]u32 = [0, 1, 524288, 1048575, 1048576, 3, 7340033, 13107200, 20000000, 24817248, 25165823, 25165824, 25165825, 30000000];
    var t : u8 = 0;
    var i : usize = 0;
    var j : usize = 0;
    var n : u32 = 0;
    var longest : u32 = 0;
    var reads : u32 = 0;
    var x : u32 = 12345;
    while (t < 4) {
        i = 0;
        while (i < 12) {
            j = 0;
            while (j < 14) {
                boot_at(0);
                r_jt = t;
                r_vg = vgs[i];
                r_vd = vds[j];
                ph = P_LIM;
                n = run_to_phase(P_ACC, 2000);
                assert_eq(r_id, id_of(tab_of(t), vgs[i], vds[j]));
                assert_eq(r_gd, gds_cell(tab_of(t), vgs[i], vds[j]));
                if (n > longest) { longest = n; }
                reads = reads + 1;
                j = j + 1;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        // 150 points of a pseudo-random sequence over the whole range and a little beyond it
        i = 0;
        while (i < 150) {
            x = lcg(x);
            const vg : u32 = (x >> 3) % 25200000;
            x = lcg(x);
            const vd : u32 = (x >> 3) % 25200000;
            boot_at(0);
            r_jt = t;
            r_vg = vg;
            r_vd = vd;
            ph = P_LIM;
            n = run_to_phase(P_ACC, 2000);
            assert_eq(r_id, id_of(tab_of(t), vg, vd));
            assert_eq(r_gd, gds_cell(tab_of(t), vg, vd));
            // the four nodes the machine fetched, through the spec's own blend and blend1
            assert_eq(r_id, blend((r_t0 as u64), (r_t1 as u64), (r_t2 as u64), (r_t3 as u64), r_fx, r_fy));
            assert_eq(r_gd, blend1(dpos((r_t2 as u64), (r_t0 as u64)), dpos((r_t3 as u64), (r_t1 as u64)), r_fx));
            if (n > longest) { longest = n; }
            reads = reads + 1;
            i = i + 1;
        }
        t = t + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(reads, 4 * (12 * 14 + 150));
    // a read is a few hundred clocks, whatever the point
    assert(longest < 300);
    assert(longest > 100);
}

test an_iteration_has_the_specs_p_n_d_and_move_at_every_step_checked {
    var ks : [8]u16 = [0, 1, 2, 57, 199, 200, 201, 399];
    var k : usize = 0;
    var maxg : u32 = 0;
    var maxd : u32 = 0;
    var iters : u32 = 0;
    while (k < 8) {
        const step : u16 = ks[k];
        boot_at(step);
        const a : u32 = gate_at((step as u32));
        const a0 : u32 = prev_gate(step);
        var y0v : u32 = REST_TT;
        if (step > 0) { y0v = TT_RUN[(step - 1) as usize]; }
        var y : u32 = y0v;
        var it : u32 = 0;
        while (it < 3) {
            run_to_phase(P_PN, 20000);
            assert_eq(r_y, y);
            assert_eq(r_sp, gq_pos(&TT_N, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, y, y0v, a, a0));
            assert_eq(r_sn, gq_neg(&TT_P, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, y, y0v, a, a0));
            assert_eq((r_sd as u64), gq_deriv(&TT_N, &TT_P, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, y, a));
            if (mag_diff(r_sp, r_sn) > maxg) { maxg = mag_diff(r_sp, r_sn); }
            if (r_sd > maxd) { maxd = r_sd; }
            run_to_phase(P_UPD, 200);
            tick();
            y = r_y;
            iters = iters + 1;
            it = it + 1;
        }
        assert_eq(st, ST_JUDGE);
        assert_eq(y, TT_RUN[step as usize]);
        k = k + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(iters, 24);
    // the divider's dividend fits 47 bits and its remainder 24: g < 2^26 and d < 2^23 on these steps (the whole run is measured below)
    assert(maxg < G_BOUND);
    assert(maxd < D_BOUND);
    assert(maxg > 1000);
}

test a_step_is_the_specs_board_step {
    var ks : [10]u16 = [0, 1, 2, 3, 57, 199, 200, 201, 300, 399];
    var k : usize = 0;
    var longest : u32 = 0;
    var n : u32 = 0;
    while (k < 10) {
        const step : u16 = ks[k];
        boot_at(step);
        n = run_to_judge();
        assert_eq(st, ST_JUDGE);
        var y0v : u32 = REST_TT;
        if (step > 0) { y0v = TT_RUN[(step - 1) as usize]; }
        assert_eq(r_y, board_step_q(&TT_N, &TT_P, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, y0v, gate_at((step as u32)), prev_gate(step)));
        assert_eq(r_y, TT_RUN[step as usize]);
        if (n > longest) { longest = n; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    // 1700 to 1960 clocks a step (about 19 us), the same for every step to within the multipliers' early exits
    assert(longest < 2200);
    assert(longest > 1800);
}

test the_ss_prediction_of_the_negative_control_is_the_specs {
    var out : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    var res : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    const s : u64 = run_fix_q(&SS_N, &SS_P, &SS_QD_N, &SS_QD_P, K_NEWTON, REST_TT, VDD, false, &out, &res);
    assert_eq(s, EXP_S_SS_Q);
    var i : usize = 0;
    var fails : u32 = 0;
    var ok : u32 = 0;
    while (i < 400) {
        const same : bool = out[i] == TT_RUN[i];
        if (same) { ok = ok + 1; } else { fails = fails + 1; }
        // PASS exactly at step 145 and from step 324
        const want : bool = i == (CTRL_PASS_AT as usize) or i >= (CTRL_SETTLED_FROM as usize);
        assert_eq(same, want);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(fails, CTRL_FAILS);
    assert_eq(ok, 400 - CTRL_FAILS);
    // the ss run is not a shifted tt run: it differs at the first step and is back at the rest value at the end
    assert(out[0] != TT_RUN[0]);
    assert_eq(out[399], REST_TT);
    assert_eq(out[324], REST_TT);
    assert(out[323] != REST_TT);
}

test the_machine_with_ss_tables_fails_exactly_the_predicted_lines {
    var out : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    var res : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    const s : u64 = run_fix_q(&SS_N, &SS_P, &SS_QD_N, &SS_QD_P, K_NEWTON, REST_TT, VDD, false, &out, &res);
    m_ss = true;
    boot_at(0);
    var k : usize = 0;
    var fails : u32 = 0;
    var passes : u32 = 0;
    while (k < 400) {
        run_to_judge();
        assert_eq(st, ST_JUDGE);
        assert_eq(stp as usize, k);
        assert_eq(r_y, out[k]);
        tick();
        assert_eq(st, ST_REPORT);
        if (out[k] == TT_RUN[k]) {
            assert_eq(verdict, V_PASS);
            passes = passes + 1;
        } else {
            assert_eq(verdict, V_FAIL);
            fails = fails + 1;
        }
        if (k == 399) { assert_eq(cs, EXP_S_SS_Q); }
        // the line is not sent here: the request for the next step is raised and taken
        fin = true;
        tick();
        k = k + 1;
    }
    m_ss = false;
    assert_eq(fails, CTRL_FAILS);
    assert_eq(passes, 400 - CTRL_FAILS);
    assert_eq(s, EXP_S_SS_Q);
}

test the_run_starts_after_lock_and_button_and_restarts_on_the_button {
    go0 = false;
    go1 = false;
    st = ST_REPORT;
    lines = 5;
    stp = 17;
    cs = 99;
    r_y = 12345;
    on_clock(false, true, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    on_clock(true, false, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    on_clock(false, false, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    assert_eq(st, ST_RUN);
    assert_eq(ph, P_STEP);
    assert_eq(lines, 0);
    assert_eq(stp, 0);
    assert_eq(cs, 0);
    assert_eq(r_y, REST_TT);
    tick();
    assert_eq(ph, P_STEP);
    tick();
    assert_eq(ph, P_STEP);
    tick();
    assert_eq(ph, P_STEP);
    tick();
    assert_eq(ph, P_JOB);
    assert_eq(r_y0, REST_TT);
    assert_eq(r_ga, 0);
    assert_eq(r_ga0, VDD);
    var k : u32 = 0;
    while (st == ST_RUN) {
        tick();
        k = k + 1;
    }
    tick();
    assert_eq(st, ST_REPORT);
    assert_eq(verdict, V_PASS);
    assert_eq(cs, TT_RUN[0] as u64);
    assert_eq(r_y, TT_RUN[0]);
    // the button again: back to step 0, line 0, the fold cleared, y at the rest value
    stp = 9;
    lines = 3;
    r_y = 777;
    on_clock(true, false, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    on_clock(true, true, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    on_clock(true, true, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    assert_eq(st, ST_REPORT);
    on_clock(true, true, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
    assert_eq(st, ST_RUN);
    assert_eq(stp, 0);
    assert_eq(lines, 0);
    assert_eq(cs, 0);
    assert_eq(r_y, REST_TT);
    assert_eq(verdict, V_FAIL);
}

test the_pins_show_the_state_one_clock_later {
    go0 = true;
    go1 = true;
    last = false;
    fin = false;
    st = ST_REPORT;
    verdict = V_PASS;
    tx_sh = 1022;
    tx_cnt = 5;
    hb = 0x08000000;
    tick();
    assert(!uart_tx);
    assert(!led_0);
    assert(led_1);
    assert(!led_2);
    assert(led_3);
    verdict = V_FAIL;
    tx_sh = 1023;
    tick();
    assert(uart_tx);
    assert(!led_1);
    assert(led_2);
    st = ST_JUDGE;
    tick();
    assert(uart_tx);
    assert(led_0);
    assert(led_1);
}

test the_receipt_segments_add_up_to_a_66_character_line {
    var n : usize = 0;
    var s : u8 = 0;
    while (s < PSP_SEGS) {
        n = n + (psp_seg_last(s) as usize) + 1;
        s = s + 1;
    }
    assert_eq(n, LINE_LEN);
    // the fields: widths, and the keys N Y E S L
    assert_eq(psp_width(1), 3);
    assert_eq(psp_width(2), 7);
    assert_eq(psp_width(3), 7);
    assert_eq(psp_width(4), 16);
    assert_eq(psp_width(5), 4);
    assert_eq(psp_key(1), 78);
    assert_eq(psp_key(2), 89);
    assert_eq(psp_key(3), 69);
    assert_eq(psp_key(4), 83);
    assert_eq(psp_key(5), 76);
    // every field sits at the top of the register: its first digit is nibble 15
    assert_eq(psp_top(1, 399, 0, 0, 0, 0) >> 52, 399);
    assert_eq(psp_top(2, 0, 25165824, 0, 0, 0) >> 36, 25165824);
    assert_eq(psp_top(3, 0, 0, 25165811, 0, 0) >> 36, 25165811);
    assert_eq(psp_top(4, 0, 0, 0, 0x0123456789ABCDEF, 0), 0x0123456789ABCDEF);
    assert_eq(psp_top(5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xABCD) >> 48, 0xABCD);
    // the longest values fit their fields: 25165824 = 0x1800000 is 7 digits, 399 = 0x18F is 3
    assert(25165824 < (1 << 28));
    assert(399 < (1 << 12));
}

test the_board_prints_400_lines_equal_to_the_specs_run_then_goes_round_again {
    var out : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    var res : [400]u32 = [0] ** 400;
    const s : u64 = run_fix_q(&TT_N, &TT_P, &TT_QD_N, &TT_QD_P, K_NEWTON, REST_TT, VDD, false, &out, &res);
    assert_eq(s, EXP_S_TT_Q);
    m_ss = false;
    boot_at(0);
    baud_div = 1;
    var buf : [72]u8 = [0] ** 72;
    var got : usize = 0;
    var line : u32 = 0;
    var ch : u8 = 0;
    var ticks : u32 = 0;
    var want : u64 = 0;
    var kk : usize = 0;
    var passes : u32 = 0;
    var maxg : u32 = 0;
    var maxd : u32 = 0;
    var seen_pn : u32 = 0;
    while (line < 402 and ticks < 20000000) {
        tick();
        ticks = ticks + 1;
        if (ph == P_PN and st == ST_RUN) {
            if (mag_diff(r_sp, r_sn) > maxg) { maxg = mag_diff(r_sp, r_sn); }
            if (r_sd > maxd) { maxd = r_sd; }
            seen_pn = seen_pn + 1;
        }
        if (st == ST_REPORT and tx_left == 9) {
            ch = ((tx_sh >> 1) & 255) as u8;
            buf[got] = ch;
            got = got + 1;
            if (ch == 10) {
                assert_eq(got, LINE_LEN);
                kk = (line % 400) as usize;
                if (kk == 0) { want = 0; }
                want = fold(want, out[kk]);
                // "T27 PSP"
                assert_eq(buf[0], 84);
                assert_eq(buf[1], 50);
                assert_eq(buf[2], 55);
                assert_eq(buf[3], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[4], 80);
                assert_eq(buf[5], 83);
                assert_eq(buf[6], 80);
                // " N=", " Y=", " E=", " S=", " L=": a space, the key, an equals sign, then the digits
                assert_eq(buf[7], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[8], 78);
                assert_eq(buf[9], 61);
                assert_eq(buf[13], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[14], 89);
                assert_eq(buf[15], 61);
                assert_eq(buf[23], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[24], 69);
                assert_eq(buf[25], 61);
                assert_eq(buf[33], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[34], 83);
                assert_eq(buf[35], 61);
                assert_eq(buf[52], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[53], 76);
                assert_eq(buf[54], 61);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 10, 3), kk as u64);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 16, 7), out[kk] as u64);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 26, 7), out[kk] as u64);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 26, 7), TT_RUN[kk] as u64);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 36, 16), want);
                assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 55, 4), line as u64);
                // " PASS\r\n"
                assert_eq(buf[59], 32);
                assert_eq(buf[60], 80);
                assert_eq(buf[61], 65);
                assert_eq(buf[62], 83);
                assert_eq(buf[63], 83);
                assert_eq(buf[64], 13);
                assert_eq(buf[65], 10);
                passes = passes + 1;
                if (kk == 399) { assert_eq(want, EXP_S_TT_Q); }
                got = 0;
                line = line + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    assert_eq(line, 402);
    assert_eq(lines, 402);
    assert_eq(passes, 402);
    // the divider's range over the whole run: g under 2^26, d under 2^23, and 3 iterations of 402 steps were seen
    assert_eq(seen_pn, 3 * 402);
    assert(maxg < G_BOUND);
    assert(maxd < D_BOUND);
    assert_eq(maxg, 1344396);
    assert_eq(maxd, 1216890);
    baud_div = BAUD_DIV;
}

test a_different_sample_prints_fail_and_the_leds_follow {
    // the ss tables in the tt top: the first step's sample differs from the spec's, so its line says FAIL
    m_ss = true;
    boot_at(0);
    baud_div = 1;
    var buf : [72]u8 = [0] ** 72;
    var got : usize = 0;
    var ch : u8 = 0;
    var ticks : u32 = 0;
    var seen : u32 = 0;
    while (seen == 0 and ticks < 1000000) {
        tick();
        ticks = ticks + 1;
        if (st == ST_REPORT and tx_left == 9) {
            ch = ((tx_sh >> 1) & 255) as u8;
            buf[got] = ch;
            got = got + 1;
            if (ch == 10) { seen = 1; }
        }
    }
    m_ss = false;
    assert_eq(seen, 1);
    assert_eq(got, LINE_LEN);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 10, 3), 0);
    // Y is the ss run's first sample (639474), E the tt run's (689233)
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 16, 7), 639474);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 26, 7), 689233);
    assert_eq(buf[59], 32);
    assert_eq(buf[60], 70);
    assert_eq(buf[61], 65);
    assert_eq(buf[62], 73);
    assert_eq(buf[63], 76);
    assert_eq(verdict, V_FAIL);
    baud_div = BAUD_DIV;
}

test a_line_ends_with_a_full_stop_bit_and_an_idle_gap_at_the_real_bit_period {
    // The real divider and no shortcut: 868 clocks a bit. The receiver is a terminal's: it hunts for a falling edge, takes the middle of the start bit, samples 8 data
    // bits and the stop bit at the middle of each bit period, and counts a stop bit read low as a framing error. Line 0 is read in full, then the first 12 bytes of line 1.
    m_ss = false;
    boot_at(0);
    baud_div = BAUD_DIV;
    const bd : u32 = BAUD_DIV as u32;
    const half : u32 = bd / 2;
    var buf : [80]u8 = [0] ** 80;
    var got : usize = 0;
    var ticks : u32 = 0;
    var prev : bool = true;
    var now : bool = true;
    var inframe : bool = false;
    var cnt : u32 = 0;
    var k : u32 = 0;
    var sh : u32 = 0;
    var rb : u32 = 0;
    var one : u32 = 1;
    var ferr : u32 = 0;
    var hi_run : u32 = 0;
    var run : u32 = 0;
    var gapseen : u32 = 0;
    while (got < 79 and ticks < 4000000) {
        tick();
        ticks = ticks + 1;
        now = uart_tx;
        if (prev and !now) {
            run = hi_run;
            hi_run = 0;
        }
        if (!inframe) {
            if (prev and !now) {
                // the idle run before the first frame of line 1 is the one that follows line 0's LF
                if (got == 66 and gapseen == 0) { gapseen = run; }
                inframe = true;
                cnt = 0;
                rb = 0;
            }
        } else {
            cnt = cnt + 1;
            if (cnt >= half and (cnt - half) % bd == 0) {
                k = (cnt - half) / bd;
                if (k == 0) {
                    if (now) {
                        ferr = ferr + 1;
                        inframe = false;
                    }
                } else if (k <= 8) {
                    if (now) {
                        sh = k - 1;
                        rb = rb | (one << sh);
                    }
                } else {
                    if (!now) { ferr = ferr + 1; }
                    buf[got] = (rb & 255) as u8;
                    got = got + 1;
                    inframe = false;
                }
            }
        }
        if (now) { hi_run = hi_run + 1; }
        prev = now;
    }
    assert_eq(got, 79);
    assert_eq(ferr, 0);
    // line 0 whole: "T27 PSP N=000 Y=00A8451 E=00A8451 S=... L=0000 PASS" CR LF
    assert_eq(buf[0], 84);
    assert_eq(buf[1], 50);
    assert_eq(buf[2], 55);
    assert_eq(buf[3], 32);
    assert_eq(buf[4], 80);
    assert_eq(buf[5], 83);
    assert_eq(buf[6], 80);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 10, 3), 0);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 16, 7), TT_RUN[0] as u64);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 26, 7), TT_RUN[0] as u64);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 36, 16), TT_RUN[0] as u64);
    assert_eq(buf[60], 80);
    assert_eq(buf[64], 13);
    assert_eq(buf[65], 10);
    // line 1 starts with the same seven characters, then " N=001"
    assert_eq(buf[66], 84);
    assert_eq(buf[67], 50);
    assert_eq(buf[68], 55);
    assert_eq(buf[69], 32);
    assert_eq(buf[70], 80);
    assert_eq(buf[71], 83);
    assert_eq(buf[72], 80);
    assert_eq(buf[73], 32);
    assert_eq(buf[74], 78);
    assert_eq(buf[75], 61);
    assert_eq(hex_at(&buf, 76, 3), 1);
    // the line was high for the LF's whole stop bit and GAP_BITS more bit times before line 1's first start bit (and the 1900 clocks of the next step)
    assert(gapseen >= (1 + (GAP_BITS as u32)) * bd);
    assert_eq(GAP_BITS, 2);
    baud_div = BAUD_DIV;
}
